{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1119","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Pavel and Triangles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pavel has several sticks with lengths equal to powers of two."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He has $$$a_0$$$ sticks of length $$$2^0 = 1$$$, $$$a_1$$$ sticks of length $$$2^1 = 2$$$, ..., $$$a_{n-1}$$$ sticks of length $$$2^{n-1}$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pavel wants to make the maximum possible number of triangles using these sticks. The triangles should have strictly positive area, each stick can be used in at most one triangle."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is forbidden to break sticks, and each triangle should consist of exactly three sticks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the maximum possible number of triangles."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 300\\,000$$$) — the number of different lengths of sticks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_0$$$, $$$a_1$$$, ..., $$$a_{n-1}$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$), where $$$a_i$$$ is the number of sticks with the length equal to $$$2^i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the maximum possible number of non-degenerate triangles that Pavel can make."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 2 2 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3 3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, Pavel can, for example, make this set of triangles (the lengths of the sides of the triangles are listed): $$$(2^0, 2^4, 2^4)$$$, $$$(2^1, 2^3, 2^3)$$$, $$$(2^1, 2^2, 2^2)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, Pavel cannot make a single triangle."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, Pavel can, for example, create this set of triangles (the lengths of the sides of the triangles are listed): $$$(2^0, 2^0, 2^0)$$$, $$$(2^1, 2^1, 2^1)$$$, $$$(2^2, 2^2, 2^2)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1119E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1119/problem/E"}